<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Taraz</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Talas (city)</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Taraz is a city in southern Kazakhstan on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-talas">Talas River</a>, one of the oldest towns of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>. Known in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> as Talas, it was a trading town of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk-road">Silk Road</a>, a seat of Turkic rulers such as the Turgesh and later the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kara-khanid-khanate">Kara-Khanids</a>, and lay near the site of the Battle of Talas in 751. In Soviet times it was called Dzhambul.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/taraz.jpg" alt="Taraz" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Yakov Fedorov · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karakhan_Mausoleum.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
